Because resolution is an intervention.

The moment you force something from:

maybe A / maybe B / maybe C

into:

it is A

you collapse possibilities, change how people behave around it, and often change the thing itself.

Sometimes that is exactly what you want. But sometimes the unresolved state is carrying value: privacy, play, imagination, deniability, surprise, optionality, courtship, creativity, even safety.

And sometimes the receiver needs to finish the pattern themselves. If I hand you every answer, I may give you information while taking away discovery.

So the deeper rule is:

Don’t resolve merely because you can. Resolve when resolution creates more value than the possibility space it destroys.

That’s why the wink works too. You could spell out exactly what ;) means.

But then it wouldn’t quite mean the same thing anymore.